# One line-ending policy for every machine (macOS/Linux/Windows dev boxes):
# text files are LF in the repo AND in every working tree, so checkouts,
# diffs, and hashes are byte-identical across machines regardless of each
# clone's core.autocrlf. Windows toolchains (rustc, cargo, PowerShell 7,
# Git Bash) all handle LF sources; no .bat/.cmd files exist in this repo.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
crates/ay-pb/tests/instances/koops_mat12_11_identity_complement_red_capacity.pbp -filter -diff -merge text eol=lf
# A detached Ed25519 signature (publish/known-red.jsonl.sig, signed by a
# rostered release machine) is 64 raw bytes: never text, whatever git's
# heuristic makes of one, or `text=auto` above could rewrite it on `git add`.
*.sig binary
# the development design notes is append-only: concurrent landings each add an entry, and
# a text merge of two entries added at the same place is a conflict that
# stopped two landings in a row (2026-10-14). Union keeps both entries, and
# merges two entries that took the same id without a conflict, so
# scripts/tests/test_land_select.py holds every DR id to one entry (DR-48).
the development design notes merge=union
